cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use trnsci in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "trnsci: a scientific computing suite for AWS Trainium via NKI"
abstract: >-
  trnsci is an umbrella for six scientific-computing libraries for AWS Trainium,
  written against the Neuron Kernel Interface (NKI): trnfft (FFT and complex
  tensors), trnblas (BLAS levels 1-3, fp64-class GEMM), trnrand (pseudo- and
  quasi-random generation), trnsolver (factorizations, eigensolvers, Krylov
  methods), trnsparse (sparse formats, SpMM, segment reductions) and trntensor
  (einsum, tensor decompositions, equivariant contractions).
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Friedman
    given-names: Scott
version: 0.2.3
date-released: "2026-11-25"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/trnsci/trnsci"
url: "https://trnsci.dev"
keywords:
  - AWS Trainium
  - NKI
  - Neuron
  - scientific computing
  - FFT
  - BLAS
  - sparse linear algebra
  - eigensolvers
  - tensor contractions
  - fp64 emulation
